{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And the sense of <b>like the apple of His eye</b> is an allusion to guarding: he says that HaShem will guard him just as a man guards his own eye. Or the word <b>אישׁ</b> may be elided: He will guard him like a man — the apple of His eye, for in general usage one speaks of an individual man, and so there are many instances."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:53.265661760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}